# No Cursor commit attribution

Never add any Cursor / AI attribution to git commits, pull requests, or commit messages.

Forbidden in commits and PRs:
- `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`
- Any other `Co-authored-by:` line for Cursor / cursoragent
- `Made-with: Cursor`
- `--trailer` flags that attribute work to Cursor

When creating commits:
- Use only the author identity already configured in git (`user.name` / `user.email`)
- Pass the commit message via HEREDOC with no attribution trailers
- Do not use `git commit --trailer` for Cursor attribution

If the environment still injects a Cursor trailer after commit, strip it before pushing (amend only when amend rules allow; otherwise create a new cleaned commit or rewrite as the user requests).
